D-04  Session A verifier is checkout-dependent
  The session A manifest pins the Git-blob SHA-256 of the qualification report.
  report at session A commit=96a1a3c bytes=21520 sha256=51a6435bd26ed87adc77a91ff37f14321a96ac03e199f85fde5e41c89141d92d crlf=0 lf=347
  report at session B commit=3c2144a bytes=20002 sha256=b2691296783c68d0c6a30b50aa0e931640e4d0b8cbb2d7abdd6a06de3f0e00c2 crlf=0 lf=412
  core.autocrlf=true
  A fresh Windows checkout normalizes the report to CRLF (21,520 blob bytes ->
  21,867 worktree bytes; sha256 51a6435b... -> 0bf23605...), so the session A
  verifier's filesystem hash no longer equals the manifest's blob hash.
  The 47 package files are unaffected because the package .gitattributes marks them
  '-text'. Reproduced in a disposable worktree: see
  reconciliation/session-a-verifier-at-own-commit.log

D-11  Byte-exactness guard in .gitattributes
  session A  commit=96a1a3c .gitattributes=b'* -text\n'
  session B  commit=3c2144a .gitattributes=b'* text=auto\n*.trx text\n*.zip binary\n*.json text\n*.md text\n*.log text\n*.patch text\n*.py text'
  Session A marks every package file '-text' (no line-ending or text conversion).
  Session B replaced that with '* text=auto', so its package files are not
  guaranteed byte-stable across checkout environments, and its manifest carries no
  hashes to detect the difference (D-02).

